    <string name="faq_question_interval_walking">What is interval walking?</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_interval_walking">Interval walking alternates between slower and faster walking phases for set durations. It helps you train with structure, vary intensity, and stay engaged without needing to sprint. This app guides each phase so you can focus on your walk.</string>
    <string name="faq_question_why_interval_walking">Why choose interval walking over steady walking or running?</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_why_interval_walking">Interval walking alternates easier and harder efforts, which may help improve fitness while feeling more manageable than a constant hard pace. It is generally lower impact than running, so it may feel easier on joints for many people. Some research suggests that when total energy expenditure is similar, walking and running can be associated with comparable cardiometabolic benefits.</string>
    <string name="faq_question_notifications">How do notifications work in this app?</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_notifications">The app supports in-app vibration and optional voice cues for phase changes. It also uses an ongoing system notification while a workout is running in the background, so Android keeps the session active and you can return quickly.</string>
    <string name="faq_question_background">Can workouts run in the background?</string>
    <string name="faq_answer_background">Yes. On supported Android versions, workouts continue when the app is backgrounded using a foreground service and notification. If you use an older Android device or aggressive battery-saving settings, you may need to exclude this app from battery optimization in system settings to improve background reliability.</string>
